Guitar UI Experience:

Introduction:

An interactive front‑end project built around guitar‑themed UI components. This page blends custom visuals, smooth animations, and reusable JavaScript modules to create a digital guitar workshop — complete with fretboard accordions, body‑style tabs, guitarist sliders, and a soundhole quote rotator.

The goal of the project is to explore UI component design, animation, and state management while maintaining a cohesive guitar‑inspired aesthetic.

Features Overview:

  Banner and Navigation -
    - Full-width guitar banner
    - Sticky navigation bar
    - Smooth scroll behavior with scroll-margin offsets
    - Active section highlighting via scroll logic


Fretboard Accordion Component:

 A custom accordion styled to resemble a guitar fretboard.

    Features:
        - Full-width fretboard pattern using repeating linear gradients
        - Metal fret bars and nut styling
        - Dot inlays (including double-dot on 12th fret)
        - Smooth open/close transitions
        - Reusable accordion logic
        - Active state toggling with custom diamond inlays

Acoustic Guitar Tabs Component:

 A reusable tab system showcasing six common acoustic guitar body styles.

    Features:
        - Semantic HTML for tab buttons and content panels
        - Shared CSS for spacing, colors, images, hover states 
          and active tabs
        - Reusable JS tab logic
            * Querying tab buttons and panels
            * Managing active states
            * Ensuring only one tab is open at a time

Electric Guitar Tabs Component:

 A parallel tab system covering six common electric guitar body styles.

    Features: 
        - Reuses the acoustic tab component logic
        - Shares styling for consistency
        - polished hover and active states

Guitarist Slider Component:

 An interactive slider featuring twelve well known guitarists, each with:
  - Signature uitar
  - Playing style
  - Musical attributes

  Slider Features:
   - Infinite looping using cloned slides
   - Auto - slide rotation
   - Pause on mouseenter/focus
   - Remove on mouseleave/blur
   - Manual prev/next button controls
   - Smooth transform transitions
   - Fade-in active slide animation
   - Responsive layout

Soundhole Rotator Component:

 A rotating quote display styled around an acoustic guitar soundhole.

Features:
   - Circular soundhole layout
   - Rotating quotes with author attribution
   - Rotating string-pin dots that are synchronized with the quote rotation
   - Pause/resume on hover
   - Smooth timing and transitions


Scroll Logic:

 Scroll based Navigation
   - Highlights active nav link based on scroll position
   - Smooth scrolling between sections
   - Scroll-margin offsets for clean section alignment

Components:

 This projects is organized around modular, reusable UI components.
    Accordion Component — fretboard‑styled headers, dot inlays, smooth height transitions

    Tab Component — shared logic for acoustic and electric sections

    Slider Component — infinite looping, auto‑slide, pause/resume logic

    Rotator Component — soundhole‑themed quote rotator with synchronized decorative elements

    Scroll Spy — highlights active sections based on scroll position

Each component is built with lightweight vanilla JS and clean, semantic HTML.

Key Learnings:

 Throughout development, this project reinforced:

   - Building reusable UI components with vanilla JavaScript

   - Managing active states across multiple interactive sections

   -  Creating custom themed UI (fretboards, soundholes, guitar silhouettes)

   - Implementing smooth animations and transitions

   - Improving accessibility with keyboard interaction and focus handling

   - Designing cohesive visual systems across multiple components

